        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          Excel worksheets show dates, OD600 measurements and graphs for analysis of growth for strain 1218R and LHM4. Two strain were used, 1218R and LHM4 strain. LHM4 is a derivative of strain 1218R. To produce LHM4 a plasmid was incorporated into the genome of 1218R. The plasmid encodes red fluorescent and kanamycin resistance. Bacteria were grown and experiments performed according to Abshire et al NPJ Microgravity (2016) 2, 16038; doi:10.1038/npjmgrav.2016.38. 
<p>
For the continuous growth studies, one large volume of OD600 0.0005 culture was prepared from an initiating tube culture and split between two 10 ml HARV: one was subjected to NG and the other to LSMMG. After 4 days the cultures were removed and the OD600 was determined. The statistical difference between the LSMMG and NG cultures was tested by a T-test performed using SAS 9.4 (SAS Inc. Gary, NC). To examine culture density during exponential growth, one large volume of OD600 0.002 culture was prepared from an initiating tube culture and split between two 50 ml HARV: one was subjected to NG and the other to LSMMG. Where specified, 3 µg catalase / ml (0.06 U/ ml) (ThermoFisher Scientific, Waltham, MA) was included. Bacteria were grown for ~150 hrs but the HARVs were stopped to remove samples (1 -2 ml). Liquid medium was added to the HARV to replace the removed sample volume (2-4% of the volume) to maintain a low shear environment. In order to obtain accurate OD600 and CFU measurements, a disaggregation procedure was used: SDS (final concentration 0.01%) was added; the culture was passed through a 27.5 gauge needle and either vortexed prior to measurement of the OD600 or preparation of dilutions. The bacteria were allowed to settle for 5 minutes prior to growth on solid medium. Use of the syringe needle, vortexing, and then allowing the culture to settle prior to plating on solid medium is standard procedure for mycobacterium. Colonies from each sample were grown on at least two plates of solid medium for 7-10 days. Colonies were counted for each time point and the CFU/ ml calculated. Preliminary experiments confirmed by microscopy that disaggregation of cultures was achieved using the syringe needle, and initial experiments determined that the addition of the SDS to the NG and LSMMG cultures only during the disaggregation and dilution stage did not alter colony forming ability (data not shown). 
<p>
To determine statistical differences between LSMMG and NG cultures during the 37-70 hour time period of growth, regression analysis was performed on the OD600 data using SAS 9.4 (SAS Inc. Gary, NC).
<p>
Period of collection ranges from November 18, 2013 to June 12, 2014.
        </div>

